      "pitch": "A German tutor for A2-C1 learners and the telc / Goethe exams that runs entirely in your browser: the weights download once, nothing you type leaves your machine.",
      "purpose": "German tutor for A2-C1 learners and the telc / Goethe exams: plans a session, drills, corrects and explains, in German or English. Trained on a verified lexicon of 3,800 nouns and 164 irregular verbs, about 1,400 engine-computed rule drills (numbers, dates, prices, clock times, contractions, verb prepositions), a rebuilt correction family - a rule kind for every classic learner error with verified bilingual rule sentences and a diff line that names the changed word - and a family of bilingual grammar rule cards (Perfekt, adjective endings, cases, word order, and from this version the C1 topics: Nominalstil, Partizipialattribut, indirect speech with Konjunktiv I, passive substitutes, two-part connectors) whose rule sentences are copied from one verified fact block and, where that block is in front of the tutor, quoted from it word for word. Teacher-written rows whose German contradicts the lexicon's gender, plural or verb forms are dropped at build time, and long answers - letters, dialogues, study plans, translations - are trained to a length budget so they end inside the browser's token limit. Asked to prepare for an everyday situation (\"train me to go to a barber shop\"), it writes a briefing - what happens, the phrases both ways with glosses, a short rehearsal - and offers to play the counterpart; asked for the role-play itself, it answers in character with one short German line and a question, from a family of engine-composed situation cards (A2-C1) whose facts are fixed.",
